<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_ScaldWater.xml                     UtinniPatches · authored 2026-09-06
  ============================================================================
  LIQUID_BIOMES_MAP_1 — OFFLINE HALF. The "boiling-lift" mechanic for the
  Scald, the crater lake at (35,185) that is the item's "boiling ocean"
  (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/ASHKARR_WORLD_DEFINITION.md §Water; region
  "Scald" in world/ASHKARR_WORLDMAP_tiles.csv, biome=Lake, MEASURED 312/312
  tiles water=1). Sits in the Anvil substellar band (arc 0-30, +70..+58 C) —
  "the hottest lake in the hottest place"
  (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/terminator_sea.md §2's own comparison
  table: "the Scald's coast ... +38 to +58 C, overhead, fierce").

  Mechanic and values lifted from
  design/Jawa/mods/REGROWTH_BOILING_LIFT_SPEC.md §R-B3/R-B4a (route (b):
  "author six TerrainDefs ... in src/Jawa/Jawa_Patches", ruled 2026-08-15,
  NEVER BUILT — measure.get confirms zero defs named Jawa_ScaldWater* exist
  in the live def dump, defs.sqlite mods=596/cec112bad2152f47,
  captured=2026-09-05T14:41:26Z). Renamed Jawa_ -> RUT_ under the
  NAMING_SCHEME_PLAN.md tier grammar (this is new authorship, not a
  migration, so it takes the new prefix directly rather than waiting on
  NAMING_SCHEME_EXECUTION_1) and rehomed from the retired src/Jawa/Jawa_Patches
  to src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches, the live successor mod
  (mandrake.rut.patches, JAWA_PATCHES_SPLIT_1).

  R-B3's five reasons to author rather than reference the ReGrowth: Boiling
  donor still hold (donor's own boiling water terrain does NOTHING — no
  hediff, no damage, no heat, identical to vanilla water bar a cyan glow;
  route (a) drags in 41 defs incl. a cut BiomeDef and 14 unwanted plants).

  ParentName safety verified by direct read of Core/Defs/TerrainDefs/
  Terrain_Water.xml: WaterDeepBase, WaterChestDeepBase and WaterShallowBase
  all carry a real Name="..." attribute on their own <TerrainDef> tag (lines
  41, 73, 103), so ParentName against them resolves — unlike Lake/Ocean/
  IceSheet (see RUT_TheScald.xml / RUT_NightsideIce.xml in this same folder
  for the trap this is NOT hitting).

  Field-by-field provenance, copied from the vanilla leaf each RUT_ScaldWater*
  def stands in for (same file, so the shape after gravship-landing and
  after a bridge crossing matches vanilla, not a truncated def):
    WaterDeep -> RUT_ScaldWaterDeep               (line 51-58)
    WaterOceanDeep -> RUT_ScaldWaterOceanDeep      (line 60-69)
    WaterMovingChestDeep -> RUT_ScaldWaterMovingChestDeep (line 85-99)
    WaterShallow -> RUT_ScaldWaterShallow          (line 114-126)
    WaterOceanShallow -> RUT_ScaldWaterOceanShallow(line 128-141)
    WaterMovingShallow -> RUT_ScaldWaterMovingShallow (line 143-161)
  gravshipReplacementTerrain is repointed within this family (deep -> our own
  shallow, never vanilla's) so a gravship landing on the Scald does not
  quietly convert boiling water back into ordinary water.

  R-B4a's boiling-lift values, applied verbatim:
    glowColor (2,154,229), glowRadius 2         — the donor's cyan, the one
                                                   thing worth keeping.
    burnDamage 3 / burnIntervalTicks 300        — shallow + moving variants.
    burnDamage 4 / burnIntervalTicks 240        — deep + chest-deep variants.
      REVISED 2026-09-26 from R-B4a's authored 1/2. Two reasons, both
      measured or ruled, neither a rebalance:
      (a) HediffGiver_Terrain applies Mathf.Max(burnDamage, 3) — MEASURED in
          the decompile (Verse/HediffGiver_Terrain.cs) — so the authored 1
          and 2 were BOTH silently 3 in play and the defs did not say what
          they did. Only the interval ever differed.
      (b) Owner ruling 2026-09-25 (scald_steam_and_hazards_spec.md §9 ruling
          9), typed: deep water should burn harder. 4 deep / 3 shallow is
          that ruling stated honestly rather than hidden under the floor.
      Still bracketed by Odyssey's HotSpring (0/0) and LavaShallow (3/120,
      Data/Odyssey/Defs/TerrainDefs/Terrain_Water.xml): the Scald now bites
      as hard as lava per hit but a half to a third as often.
    traversedThought HotSpring                  — Odyssey's own ThoughtDef,
      already loaded (Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey is active), reused rather than
      SoakingWet.
    avoidWander true                            — pawns should not idle in it.
    RUT_ScaldShallow tag ADDED (SCALD_MECHANICS_1 S6 build pass, 2026-09-13)
      to the three shallow variants only (RUT_ScaldWaterShallow/
      OceanShallow/MovingShallow) — scald_kit_spec.md §S6's own resolved
      finding: stock GenStep_ScatterThings.CanScatterAt is TAG-based, not
      defName-based, so the burning-shallows wreck scatter needs exactly one
      shared tag on these three terrains and zero new C#. Deep/chest-deep
      variants do NOT carry it — wrecks sit in the shallows, per the sheet's
      own §8 text, not the boil's open water.
    dbh_water tag REMOVED (SCALD_MECHANICS_1 spike, 2026-09-13) — R-B4a's
      own caveat ("verify against DBH's own reader before relying on it")
      is now resolved: BadHygiene.dll (workshop/294100/836308268, 1.6
      Assemblies) carries both the `dbh_water` literal and the thirst
      drink-tracking strings (DrankCleanWater/DrankDirtyWater/DrinkCount) in
      the same assembly, and this file's OWN prior header already stated the
      intended behaviour outright: "without this tag DBH will not treat this
      as a drinkable... water source" — i.e. the tag was placed here
      specifically so pawns COULD drink the boil. That is a direct conflict
      with the_scald.md's frozen Ban 1 ("never potable... only its distilled
      breath"), which governs this kit. Ban 1 wins (it is the later, frozen
      lore ruling; R-B4a's "water is currency" economy is satisfied instead
      by S2's steam-catch condenser and S3's margin ring). The tag now lives
      ONLY on `RUT_ScaldMargin` (RUT_ScaldMargin.xml, this kit's S3) — the
      one cool ring where pawns can actually drink and bathe; these six boil
      terrains carry no drink route at all, matching scald_kit_spec.md §6
      row 1's own pre-ruled remedial action.
    waterBodyType Saltwater + Ocean tag          — ocean-shallow/ocean-deep
      variants only, matching vanilla's own WaterOceanDeep/WaterOceanShallow
      pattern. The Lake-facing variants (Deep/Shallow/MovingShallow/
      MovingChestDeep) keep the inherited Freshwater default: no design doc
      calls the Scald basin itself saline (unlike the two terminator brine
      seas, terminator_sea.md), so this is NOT changed here — flagged as an
      open question for the owner in the design note this item also writes
      (LIQUID_BIOMES_MAP_1_RECONCILIATION.md), not decided unilaterally.

  What this file does NOT do: assign these terrains to the Scald's world
  tiles. That is RUT_TheScald.xml's job (a BiomeDef, painted onto the 312
  Scald tiles only via the LIVE, owner-gated half of this item) — these are
  just the terrain defs themselves, which parse and validate standalone.

  ============================================================================
  TERMINALBIOMES_LIQUID_RETARGET_1 (Q7 ownership ruling execution,
  2026-09-28) — investigated, NOT repointed. Reasoning:
  ============================================================================
  LIQUID_TERRAIN_AUTHORED_TWICE_1 (closed 2026-09-27) already found and
  fixed the one real fork in this family: FlowWorks' generic
  RM_WaterBoilingShallow/Deep still carried R-B4a's original burn 1/2 while
  these six had been ruled to 3/4 on 2026-09-25/26. Fix applied there was to
  sync generate_liquid_suite.py's boiling row to 3/300 shallow, 4/240 deep
  and regenerate RM_WaterBoiling.xml — the NUMBERS now agree everywhere.
  That item explicitly declined to repoint or delete this file, and
  Q7's ownership ruling does not change that answer: FlowWorks' generated
  suite only ever covers two variants (Shallow/Deep); it has no Ocean,
  Moving-shallow or Moving-chest-deep rows at all (the generator's own
  declared scope). The Scald genuinely needs all six — RM_TheScald.xml and
  the frozen save-compat twin RUT_TheScald.xml both pin all six defNames by
  name across waterDeepTerrain/waterShallowTerrain/waterMovingShallowTerrain/
  waterMovingChestDeepTerrain/<coastal> — plus per-variant tuning FlowWorks'
  generic suite does not carry at all: gravshipReplacementTerrain routing,
  the RUT_ScaldShallow tag the wreck-scatter GenStep reads (tag-based, not
  defName-based — RUT_ScaldWreckScatter.xml, unaffected either way), and the
  SCALD_WATER_AGITATION_FLECKS_1 steam fleck tuning. This is a biome-specific
  formation family that happens to share a substance name with FlowWorks'
  generic pair, not a duplicate of it. Nothing here is orphaned; nothing was
  retargeted. Do not re-open this a third time on a defName-similarity read
  alone.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <TerrainDef ParentName="WaterDeepBase">
    <defName>RUT_ScaldWaterDeep</defName>
    <label>deep boiling water</label>
    <description>Deep water at the boil, kept liquid by heat rather than by depth. It is dead calm on the surface and scalding underneath — nothing swims here that cannot stand the temperature, and nothing wades in without paying for it.</description>
    <renderPrecedence>395</renderPrecedence>
    <texturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/WaterDeepRamp</texturePath>
    <pollutedTexturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/WaterDeepRampPolluted</pollutedTexturePath>
    <forcePassableByFlyingPawns>true</forcePassableByFlyingPawns>
    <gravshipReplacementTerrain>RUT_ScaldWaterShallow</gravshipReplacementTerrain>
    <glowColor>(2,154,229)</glowColor>
    <glowRadius>2</glowRadius>
    <burnDamage>4</burnDamage>
    <burnIntervalTicks>240</burnIntervalTicks>
    <!-- SCALD_WATER_AGITATION_FLECKS_1 / scald_steam_and_hazards_spec.md
         §3.1 step 2, 2026-09-26: steam standing off the boil, zero C#.
         SteadyEnvironmentEffects visits ceil(area*0.0006) cells per tick
         (MEASURED in the decompile) and rolls throwFleckChance on each, so
         every cell is offered a puff about once per 1667 ticks; at 0.75 a
         deep cell breathes roughly every 35 s and a screenful of open boil
         carries a steady haze. Shape copied from Odyssey's own HotSpring
         block (fleck AirPuff, solidTicksRange 1~3), but angled upward
         (-30~30, not -90~90) and larger, because this water is boiling
         rather than merely warm, and set far above HotSpring's 0.25 on the
         owner's walk verdict that the Scald read nearly flat. -->
    <fleckData>
      <fleck>AirPuff</fleck>
      <velocitySpeedRange>0.2~0.6</velocitySpeedRange>
      <velocityAngleRange>-30~30</velocityAngleRange>
      <rotationSpeedRange>-20~20</rotationSpeedRange>
      <solidTicksRange>1~3</solidTicksRange>
      <scaleRange>2~4</scaleRange>
    </fleckData>
    <throwFleckChance>0.75</throwFleckChance>
    <traversedThought>HotSpring</traversedThought>
    <avoidWander>true</avoidWander>
    <tags>
      <li>Water</li>
      <li>RM_WaterAgitationHeavy</li>
    </tags>
  </TerrainDef>

